    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `displayName` on the owner response, formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. Since the response DTO (`OwnerDto`) is generated from this spec at build time, this gives it a `displayName` getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 populated it in the MapStruct `toOwnerDto(Owner)` mapping via an expression: `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()`. Because both the create-response (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and GET flows map through `toOwnerDto`, the field is computed from the persisted entity's names in every response.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` (POST an owner, then GET it and assert `$.displayName == \"LastName, John\"`) passes, and the full suite builds green.",
